1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,772
Ravi's second Chai Corner
has been open for one month.

2
00:00:04,072 --> 00:00:06,526
The plan was five hundred cups a day.

3
00:00:06,526 --> 00:00:07,848
But is it working?

4
00:00:08,398 --> 00:00:11,204
Some cups are full, and
some are half empty.

5
00:00:11,504 --> 00:00:14,394
Some customers wait one
minute, and some wait five.

6
00:00:14,694 --> 00:00:17,672
And nobody has counted the cups even once.

7
00:00:18,322 --> 00:00:21,031
A plan nobody checks is just a guess.

8
00:00:21,031 --> 00:00:22,690
Ravi needs controlling.

9
00:00:23,390 --> 00:00:24,828
So, what is controlling?

10
00:00:25,128 --> 00:00:29,298
Controlling means checking that the
actual work matches the plan, and fixing

11
00:00:29,298 --> 00:00:30,540
it when it doesn't.

12
00:00:31,140 --> 00:00:34,089
First, compare the plan
with what really happened.

13
00:00:34,089 --> 00:00:35,497
Then, close the gap.

14
00:00:36,147 --> 00:00:38,163
Controlling follows five steps.

15
00:00:38,613 --> 00:00:39,513
One.

16
00:00:39,115 --> 00:00:41,123
Set standards: clear targets.

17
00:00:41,123 --> 00:00:45,778
Every cup holds a hundred and fifty
millilitres, the wait stays under ninety

18
00:00:45,778 --> 00:00:48,406
seconds, and the taste stays the same.

19
00:00:48,756 --> 00:00:49,656
Two.

20
00:00:49,279 --> 00:00:51,104
Measure actual performance.

21
00:00:51,104 --> 00:00:53,728
Every evening, Kabir counts the cups.

22
00:00:53,728 --> 00:00:56,261
Outlet two sells four hundred a day.

23
00:00:56,611 --> 00:00:57,511
Three.

24
00:00:57,170 --> 00:00:58,810
Compare with the standard.

25
00:00:58,810 --> 00:01:02,209
The goal was five hundred,
so it is one hundred short.

26
00:01:02,559 --> 00:01:03,459
Four.

27
00:01:03,102 --> 00:01:06,635
Analyse the deviation, the
gap between plan and actual.

28
00:01:06,635 --> 00:01:08,373
Twenty percent fewer cups.

29
00:01:08,373 --> 00:01:09,273
Why?

30
00:01:08,868 --> 00:01:13,061
At the morning rush, one stove
is not enough, and people leave.

31
00:01:13,411 --> 00:01:14,311
Five.

32
00:01:13,988 --> 00:01:15,615
Take corrective action.

33
00:01:15,615 --> 00:01:19,961
Ravi adds a second stove, and
sales climb back to five hundred.

34
00:01:20,611 --> 00:01:22,259
Then the loop starts again.

35
00:01:22,609 --> 00:01:24,519
Next month, Kabir counts again.

36
00:01:24,519 --> 00:01:27,817
This is a feedback loop:
check, fix, and check again.

37
00:01:28,467 --> 00:01:31,103
Planning and controlling
always go together.

38
00:01:31,453 --> 00:01:32,927
Planning sets the target.

39
00:01:32,927 --> 00:01:34,841
Controlling checks if you hit it.

40
00:01:35,191 --> 00:01:37,797
Without a plan, there is nothing to check.

41
00:01:37,797 --> 00:01:40,313
Without checking, a plan is just a wish.

42
00:01:40,663 --> 00:01:44,121
That's why they are called the
Siamese twins of management.

43
00:01:44,771 --> 00:01:47,487
But Ravi cannot check
every small thing himself.

44
00:01:47,837 --> 00:01:50,186
So he uses management by exception.

45
00:01:50,536 --> 00:01:54,632
Small slips, like a cup that is a
little short, are fixed by the team.

46
00:01:54,982 --> 00:01:59,533
Only big deviations, like sales
falling twenty percent, reach Ravi.

47
00:01:59,883 --> 00:02:02,713
Frederick Taylor called this
the exception principle.

48
00:02:03,363 --> 00:02:04,372
Quick check.

49
00:02:04,372 --> 00:02:08,659
Kabir only calls Ravi when sales
drop by more than ten percent.

50
00:02:08,659 --> 00:02:10,157
Which idea is this?

51
00:02:12,057 --> 00:02:13,704
Management by exception!

52
00:02:13,704 --> 00:02:16,403
Only the big problems reach the manager.

53
00:02:17,003 --> 00:02:18,012
So, remember.

54
00:02:18,312 --> 00:02:22,875
Controlling checks that actual work
matches the plan, and fixes the gap.

55
00:02:23,225 --> 00:02:27,927
It has five steps: set standards,
measure, compare, analyse, and correct.

56
00:02:28,277 --> 00:02:33,145
Planning and controlling are twins, and
managers focus on the big exceptions.

57
00:02:33,745 --> 00:02:38,966
Next time, Ravi and his team set goals
together, with management by objectives.
